<title>CHINA: China bank in 53.6 bln yuan loans for spring crops.</title>
<headline>China bank in 53.6 bln yuan loans for spring crops.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agricultural Bank of China has extended a total of 53.6 billion yuan ($6.46 billion) in loans to finance the current spring sowing, the Economic Daily said on Thursay.</p>
<p>The loans were up by 15.9 billion yuan compared with the same period last year, it said.</p>
<p>Local branches of the bank have given priority to spring farm production and to measures to meet farmers' demand for capital, it said.</p>
<p>Bank branches boosted loans to farmers in northern China to finance their purchase of irrigation equipment to fight a continuing drought, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
